#     - Discord: https://discord.com/developers/applications
# [ ] Configure localhost callback URLs in OAuth apps
# [ ] Copy this template to .env.development.local
# [ ] Replace all REPLACE_WITH_* values
# [ ] Run database migrations
# [ ] Seed test data
# [ ] Test OAuth flows with each provider
# [ ] Verify PKCE and CSRF protection

# ================================================================
# 📝 OAUTH PROVIDER SETUP FOR DEVELOPMENT
# ================================================================

# Google OAuth Setup for Development:
# 1. Go to Google Cloud Console
# 2. Create a new project or use existing
# 3. Enable Google+ API
# 4. Create OAuth 2.0 Client ID (Web application)
# 5. Add authorized redirect URIs:
#    - http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/oauth/google/callback
#    - http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1/auth/oauth/google/callback
# 6. Copy Client ID and Secret to this config

# GitHub OAuth Setup for Development:
# 1. Go to GitHub Settings > Developer settings > OAuth Apps
# 2. Create New OAuth App
# 3. Set authorization callback URL:
#    - http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/oauth/github/callback
# 4. Copy Client ID and generate Client Secret

# Discord OAuth Setup for Development:
# 1. Go to Discord Developer Portal
# 2. Create New Application
# 3. Go to OAuth2 section
# 4. Add redirect URI:
#    - http://localhost:8000/api/v1/auth/oauth/discord/callback
# 5. Copy Client ID and Client Secret

# ================================================================
# 🚀 DEVELOPMENT QUICK START COMMANDS
# ================================================================

# Start development services with Docker:
# docker-compose -f docker-compose.dev.yml up -d

# Run the application:
# uvicorn app.main:app --reload --host 0.0.0.0 --port 8000

# Run tests:
# pytest tests/ -v

# Run OAuth security validation:
# python security/oauth-security-validator-enhanced.py

# Run OAuth testing framework:
# python security/oauth-testing-framework.py --base-url http://localhost:8000

